 "notes": "Nineteen screens: home, locations, containers, inventory, supply types and settings were seen on the device; the rest are from code. The unknown-barcode dialog and the supply type sheet are counted because each makes a choice or holds a form; the overflow menu, delete confirmations and the unreachable supply list are not. Register and Add screens (and Duplicate, which opens Add supply prefilled) are creation, and the move screens are each thing's own sub-flow, so no thing is edited outside its home. One step per tap, typing a field is one step, pointing the scanner after its button is part of that step. Scenarios assume the places and supplies were logged with a camera, which the walk could not do. R09 opens the cabinet from the flat container list (2 taps; from the location list also 2). R11 uses containers as the groups and moves one supply at a time by scanning the destination; the fewest-tap reading assumes the bottom-bar Scan is on detail screens and Move Supply returns to the container, and scanning is not recall because the label is in front of the user. R05 is null (no tags; a type's one category changes every instance), R06-R08 null (one photo, no recognition), R10 null (nesting and a top-level location filter, but no map and no fallback list), R114 and R115 null (pack sizes but no prices)."
